+
+# QNX port: EXTRA_PROTO_TARGETS above (and PROTOBUF_CMAKE_MAPPING's original 4 entries) are
+# only actually applied when protobuf is FetchContent-vendored and its own real BUILD files are
+# processed by bazel_to_cmake. With TENSORSTORE_USE_SYSTEM_PROTOBUF=ON, that whole path is
+# skipped (early return in third_party_http_archive.py before "bazel_to_cmake"/"args" is ever
+# read), so callers referencing e.g. "@com_google_protobuf//:duration_proto" or its
+# __cpp_library/__upb_library/__upbdefs_library/__minitable_library variants get an unresolved
+# target error -- exactly what this module's own docstring says should NOT happen ("when using
+# system protobuf, the well_known_proto_types are available via protobuf::libprotobuf"). This
+# extends PROTOBUF_CMAKE_MAPPING (the one thing that *does* survive the system-package early
+# return) to actually deliver on that comment: every well-known-type proto target, in every
+# generated variant, redirects to the same protobuf::libprotobuf the system protobuf install
+# already provides (which already contains the compiled-in well-known types). See
+# project_tensorstore_qnx.md for the full investigation.
+PROTOBUF_CMAKE_MAPPING.update({
+    "//:" + x + "_proto" + y: "protobuf::libprotobuf"
+    for x in WELL_KNOWN_TYPES
+    for y in SUFFIXES
+})
+
